# Files excluded from the EAS build upload (gitignore syntax). None of these
# are imported by the app, so they never reach the binary — this just keeps the
# upload lean and removes any chance of accidental bundling.

# Docs & handoff notes
TEST_REPORT.md
SMOKE_TEST.md
GOSPELS_PSALMS_PLAN.md
COMMENTARY_CDN_HANDOFF.md
BADGES_FILELIST.txt
FONTS.md

# Dev-only test harness (jest) — not part of the app runtime
__tests__/
test/
jest.config.js

# One-off export deliverables (mood emoji PNGs were generated for the user,
# not used by the app)
mood_emoji_png/

# Data-pipeline source folders (already gitignored; listed for safety)
_incoming_verses/
_cdn_ready/

# Stray build artifacts
*.aab
*.apk

# Local toolchain / caches. These are gitignored, but because a .easignore
# exists EAS ignores .gitignore entirely and uses ONLY this file — so anything
# gitignored that isn't ALSO listed here gets uploaded. `.jdk17/` is a local
# 310 MB JDK (EAS provides its own), which is what bloated the archive to 189 MB.
.jdk17/
.expo/
.gradle/
.kotlin/

# Native projects — this app is managed / CNG (config plugins in app.json).
# A leftover local android/ or ios/ from a manual `expo prebuild` / `run:*`
# must NOT be uploaded: if EAS receives a native dir it treats the build as
# bare and SKIPS prebuild, so app.json + plugin changes (AdMob IDs, Firebase,
# ATT, Google sign-in URL scheme, app name) would be silently ignored. Keeping
# these out forces EAS to prebuild fresh from app.json on every build.
/android
/ios
play-service-account.json
